age of seventeen. He is set to star next in historical drama \"\"My Country\"\". Yang Se-jong Yang Se-jong (born ) is a South Korean actor and model. He worked as a fashion model in 2011 for a", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 301, "prompt_tokens": 274, "completion_tokens": 77, "retrieval_scores": [0.8584455847740173, 0.8532063961029053, 0.8358045220375061]}, {"t": 2, "action_type": "answer", "query_or_answer": "Yang Seung-ho", "obs_digest": "", "draft": "Yang Seung-ho", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 1.0, "raw_len": 364, "prompt_tokens": 866, "completion_tokens": 93, "retrieval_scores": []}], "answered_at": 2, "forced_stop": false, "final_answer": "Yang Seung-ho", "final_f1": 1.0, "final_em": 1.0, "steps_used": 2, "total_steps_run": 2, "rollout": 0}
{"task_id": "5ab5e14f554299494045f099", "question": "What nationality was the author of Black Earth: The Holocaust as History and Warning?", "arm": "a3", "mode": "none", "budget_B": 2, "seed": 42, "config_hash": "7e4648315a26", "steps": [{"t": 1, "action_type": "search", "query_or_answer": "author of Black Earth The Holocaust as History and Warning", "obs_digest": "[1] Black Earth: The Holocaust as History and Warning: Black Earth: The Holocaust as History and Warning Black Earth: The Holocaust as History and Warning is a 2015 book by historian Timothy D. Snyder. \"\"Black Earth\"\" offers a \"\"radically new explanation\"\" of the Holocaust. The title is drawn from the fertile black earth of Ukraine, the region where Adolf Hitler planned to replace the population with Germans, giving the German \"\"race\"\" new \"\"living space\"\" (). Race, and the idea of the world as a space in which races compete and stronger races replace weaker ones, was, according to Snyder, central to Hitler's thinking. Hitler, according to Snyder, was not\n[2] Black Earth: The Holocaust as History and Warning: the Jews. The book began to excite controversy as soon as it was published. Black Earth: The Holocaust as History and Warning Black Earth: The Holocaust as History and Warning is a 2015 book by historian Timothy D. Snyder. \"\"Black Earth\"\" offers a \"\"radically new explanation\"\" of the Holocaust. The title is drawn from the fertile black earth of Ukraine, the region where Adolf Hitler planned to replace the population with Germans, giving the German \"\"race\"\" new \"\"living space\"\" (). Race, and the idea of the world as a space in which races compete and stronger races replace weaker ones,\n[3] Arno J. Mayer: while Guttenplan described their \"\"distortion\"\" of Mayer's views as \"\"disgraceful\"\", going on to note that Reviewers criticized Mayer's account of the Holocaust as focused too heavily on Nazi anti-communism at the expense of a focus on antisemitism. Israeli historian Yehuda Bauer alleged that Much of the controversy around \"\"Why Did the Heavens Not Darken?\"\" was due to the simple fact that through this book the general public first learned of the functionalist view that there was no masterplan for the Holocaust going back to the days when Hitler wrote \"\"Mein Kampf.\"\" Timothy Snyder's \"\"Black Earth: The Holocaust as History and", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 312, "prompt_tokens": 265, "completion_tokens": 71, "retrieval_scores": [0.8949540853500366, 0.892073392868042, 0.8515092730522156]}, {"t": 2, "action_type": "search", "query_or_answer": "Timothy D. Snyder nationality", "obs_digest": "[1] Timothy D. Snyder: Timothy D. Snyder Timothy David Snyder (born 1969) is an American author and historian specializing in the history of Central and Eastern Europe, and the Holocaust. He is the Richard C. Levin Professor of History at Yale University and a Permanent Fellow at the Institute for Human Sciences in Vienna. Snyder is a member of the Council on Foreign Relations and the Committee on Conscience of the United States Holocaust Memorial Museum. Snyder was born on August 18, 1969, in southwestern Ohio, the son of Christine (Hadley), a homemaker, and Estel Eugene Snyder, a veterinarian. Snyder graduated from Centerville High\n[2] Timothy D. Snyder: Snyder has been married to Marci Shore, a professor of European cultural and intellectual history at Yale University. Snyder and Shore have two children together. Timothy D. Snyder Timothy David Snyder (born 1969) is an American author and historian specializing in the history of Central and Eastern Europe, and the Holocaust. He is the Richard C. Levin Professor of History at Yale University and a Permanent Fellow at the Institute for Human Sciences in Vienna. Snyder is a member of the Council on Foreign Relations and the Committee on Conscience of the United States Holocaust Memorial Museum. Snyder was born\n[3] Timothy Law Snyder: office as LMU's president on June 1, 2015 and was inaugurated on October 6, 2015. He is the second layperson president of LMU. Snyder was born in 1959 to Shirley and Gordon Snyder in Toledo, Ohio. He attended local public schools, including Rogers High School. Snyder is a convert to Roman Catholicism. He has an older sister, Linda Markowiak (née Snyder), and a younger brother, Scott Snyder. He has been a musician most of his life, and was the lead singer in the touring rock and punk band Whirlwind from 1976 to 1983. Despite being from Ohio, he is an", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 243, "prompt_tokens": 813, "completion_tokens": 59, "retrieval_scores": [0.8446685075759888, 0.8421239852905273, 0.8275464773178101]}, {"t": 3, "action_type": "answer", "query_or_answer": "American", "obs_digest": "", "draft": "American", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 1.0, "raw_len": 231, "prompt_tokens": 1346, "completion_tokens": 55, "retrieval_scores": []}], "answered_at": 3, "forced_stop": false, "final_answer": "American", "final_f1": 1.0, "final_em": 1.0, "steps_used": 3, "total_steps_run": 3, "rollout": 0}
{"task_id": "5ab939a5554299131ca422d1", "question": "Paramount Famous Productions is a made-for-home entertainment division of Paramount Pictures, it develops home entertainment sequels to films from which theatrical motion picture production arm, of the American children's cable channel Nickelodeon?", "arm": "a3", "mode": "none", "budget_B": 2, "seed": 42, "config_hash": "7e4648315a26", "steps": [{"t": 1, "action_type": "search", "query_or_answer": "Nickelodeon theatrical motion picture production arm", "obs_digest": "[1] Nickelodeon: films produced by the network's Nickelodeon Movies film production division (whose films are distributed by sister company Paramount Pictures). Although the film division bears the Nickelodeon brand name, the channel does not have access to most of the movies produced by its film unit. Nickelodeon does have broadcast rights to most feature films based on or that served as the basis for original series produced by it (such as \"\"Barnyard: The Original Party Animals\"\"); the majority of the live-action feature films produced under the Nickelodeon Movies banner are licensed for broadcast by various free-to-air and pay television outlets within the\n[2] Nickelodeon Movies: Nickelodeon Movies Nickelodeon Movies is the theatrical motion picture production arm of the American children's cable channel Nickelodeon. Founded in 1996, the company released its first film \"\"Harriet the Spy\"\" in 1996. It has produced family features and films based on Nickelodeon programs, as well as other adaptations and original projects. Its films are co-produced and/or distributed by Viacom division Paramount Pictures. The studio's highest-grossing films are \"\"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles\"\" (2014), which grossed $493.3 million worldwide, \"\"The Adventures of Tintin\"\" (2011), which grossed $374 million worldwide, and \"\"\"\" (2015), which grossed $323.4 million worldwide. In 1993, Nickelodeon forged a\n[3] Nickelodeon Animation Studio: water into the air. The Nicktoons studio houses five, project driven production units. Each has its own color and design environment and includes a living room, writer's lounge, and storyboard conference room. The studio also has a Foley stage (for recording live sound effects), a post-production area, sound editing and mixing rooms and an upstairs loft area with skylights for colorists. In September 1999, Nickelodeon opened a major new digital animation studio at 1633 Broadway in Manhattan. The New York studio primarily took over production of Nick Jr. ", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 379, "prompt_tokens": 290, "completion_tokens": 74, "retrieval_scores": [0.8468400835990906, 0.839648425579071, 0.8367272615432739]}, {"t": 2, "action_type": "answer", "query_or_answer": "Nickelodeon Movies", "obs_digest": "", "draft": "Nickelodeon Movies", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 1.0, "raw_len": 323, "prompt_tokens": 866, "completion_tokens": 72, "retrieval_scores": []}], "answered_at": 2, "forced_stop": false, "final_answer": "Nickelodeon Movies", "final_f1": 1.0, "final_em": 1.0, "steps_used": 2, "total_steps_run": 2, "rollout": 0}
{"task_id": "5ab94278554299743d22ea8f", "question": "What movie does Ed Skrein act in that is a french action film?", "arm": "a3", "mode": "none", "budget_B": 2, "seed": 42, "config_hash": "7e4648315a26", "steps": [{"t": 1, "action_type": "search", "query_or_answer": "Ed Skrein French action film", "obs_digest": "[1] Ed Skrein: Toom making his directorial debut. Filming will commence in Estonia in the spring of 2016. On 29 October 2015 Skrein was cast in psychological revenge thriller, \"\"In Darkness\"\", alongside Natalie Dormer and Stacy Martin; principal photography will begin early 2016. He was slated to star in the upcoming \"\"Hellboy\"\" reboot as Ben Daimio, a Japanese-American character; after controversy over his casting, Skrein announced on Twitter that he was stepping down from the role in the hopes an actor of the proper ethnicity would be cast. Skrein lives in London with his partner and his son Marley. Since he was 15\n[2] Ed Skrein: painting. In 2004, Skrein released a three track EP under the record label Dented Records. In 2007, he released his first album, \"\"The Eat Up\"\". He has collaborated with a variety of artists including Foreign Beggars, Asian Dub Foundation, Plan B, Dubbledge and Doc Brown. Later that year, Skrein released a collaborative EP, \"\"Pre-Emptive Nostalgia\"\", with the group A State of Mind. In 2009 Skrein collaborated with rapper Dr Syntax to bring the collaborative album \"\"Scene Stealers\"\" under the name Skreintax. Skrein made his acting debut in Plan B's short film \"\"Michelle\"\". Skrein got his first lead role in Plan\n[3] Ed Skrein: B's \"\"Ill Manors\"\". Skrein portrayed Daario Naharis in the third season of the television series \"\"Game of Thrones\"\". However, in the fourth season of the series, he was replaced by Dutch actor Michiel Huisman. Skrein states that it was not his choice to leave the show. In 2014, Skrein was cast in \"\"\"\", replacing Jason Statham as the lead. Though the film was critically panned, his performance was praised. In 2016, Skrein played the lead villain, Ajax, in the blockbuster action film \"\"Deadpool\"\". On 23 October 2015 Skrein was cast in sci-fi thriller, \"\"Gateway 6\"\", alongside Rhys Ifans, with Tanel", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 304, "prompt_tokens": 264, "completion_tokens": 84, "retrieval_scores": [0.8177489042282104, 0.8084135055541992, 0.8083013296127319]}, {"t": 2, "action_type": "search", "query_or_answer": "\"In Darkness\" 2015 film genre French", "obs_digest": "[1] In Darkness (2018 film): In Darkness (2018 film) In Darkness is a 2018 thriller film directed by Anthony Byrne and written by Byrne and Natalie Dormer. It stars Dormer, Emily Ratajkowski, Ed Skrein, Joely Richardson, Neil Maskell, James Cosmo and Jan Bijvoet. The film was released direct-to-video on 25 May 2018 in the United States by Vertical Entertainment and on 6 July 2018 in the United Kingdom by Shear Entertainment. Blind pianist Sofia (Natalie Dormer) overhears a struggle in the apartment above hers that leads to the death of her neighbor Veronique (Emily Ratajkowski). It is the start of a journey that pulls Sofia\n[2] In the Shadow (2010 film): In the Shadow (2010 film) In the Shadow is a 2010 French horror film written by Seb Lecocq and directed by Paul Özcan, it stars Maximilien Poullein, Jordan Jones and Emmanuelle Coutellier. Three criminology students visit the site of the murders perpetrated by an infamous serial killer. They intend to collect proof on film for a final document paper. The film is produced by Shiba Inu Production and is the Directorial debut film for French-Turkish filmmaker Paul Özcan, the shooting began on February 16, 2010 in Paris. In the Shadow is the first feature film for the Franco-Canadian producer Jimmy\n[3] Daughters of Darkness: preys cunningly on narcissistic youth, and seductiveness and cruelty become indistinguishable as Seyrig forces the innocents to become aware of their own capacity for monstrous behavior. If Fassbinder had made a vampire movie it might have looked something like this. In the early 2010s, \"\"Time Out\"\" conducted a poll with several authors, directors, actors and critics who have worked within the horror genre to vote for their top horror films. \"\"Daughters of Darkness\"\" placed at number 90 on their top 100 list. Daughters of Darkness Daughters of Darkness (in France, Les Lèvres Rouges, in Belgium, Le Rouge aux Lèvres (the", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 480, "prompt_tokens": 875, "completion_tokens": 116, "retrieval_scores": [0.839653491973877, 0.8322516679763794, 0.8321971893310547]}, {"t": 3, "action_type": "answer", "query_or_answer": "In Darkness", "obs_digest": "", "draft": "In Darkness", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 667, "prompt_tokens": 1520, "completion_tokens": 152, "retrieval_scores": []}], "answered_at": 3, "forced_stop": false, "final_answer": "In Darkness", "final_f1": 0.0, "final_em": 0.0, "steps_used": 3, "total_steps_run": 3, "rollout": 0}
{"task_id": "5aba8fd755429901930fa833", "question": "Which musical festival features The Big Golden Guitar and coincides with Australia day?", "arm": "a3", "mode": "none", "budget_B": 2, "seed": 42, "config_hash": "7e4648315a26", "steps": [{"t": 1, "action_type": "search", "query_or_answer": "Big Golden Guitar festival Australia Day", "obs_digest": "[1] Golden Guitar: Golden Guitar The Big Golden Guitar is one of the many \"\"big\"\" attractions that can be found around Australia. Located in Tamworth, New South Wales, the monument is one of the best-known points of interest in New England, New South Wales. It is also a major attraction during the Tamworth Country Music Festival. The Golden Guitar was erected in front of the famous Longyard Hotel on the Sydney Road in 1988. It was unveiled by Australia's most popular country music artist, Slim Dusty. Its location in Tamworth is symbolic of the city's recognition and celebration of Australian country music, and\n[2] Golden Guitar: during the Tamworth Country Music Festival. Golden Guitar The Big Golden Guitar is one of the many \"\"big\"\" attractions that can be found around Australia. Located in Tamworth, New South Wales, the monument is one of the best-known points of interest in New England, New South Wales. It is also a major attraction during the Tamworth Country Music Festival. The Golden Guitar was erected in front of the famous Longyard Hotel on the Sydney Road in 1988. It was unveiled by Australia's most popular country music artist, Slim Dusty. Its location in Tamworth is symbolic of the city's recognition and\n[3] Big Day Out: Big Day Out The Big Day Out was an annual music festival that was held in five Australian cities: Sydney, Melbourne, Gold Coast, Adelaide and Perth, as well as Auckland, New Zealand. The festival was held during summer, typically in January of each year but was sometimes held as late as early February in some cities including Perth. The event was conceptualised after the Violent Femmes announced a tour of Australia. Promoters Ken West and Vivian Lees sought another act as middle-level support for the band's tour. They succeeded in securing Nirvana to play the Sydney leg at Horden Pavilion.", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 286, "prompt_tokens": 264, "completion_tokens": 63, "retrieval_scores": [0.8544157147407532, 0.8520119786262512, 0.8325189352035522]}, {"t": 2, "action_type": "search", "query_or_answer": "Tamworth Country Music Festival Australia Day", "obs_digest": "[1] Tamworth Country Music Festival: Tamworth Country Music Festival The Tamworth Country Music Festival is an annual music festival in January held in Tamworth, New South Wales, Australia and is a celebration of Country Music culture and heritage in particular the national Australian country music scene, with numerous concerts and live performances at various venues. The festival lasts for two weeks over Australia Day and during this period the city of Tamworth comes alive, with visitors from all across the country and worldwide who come to join in the festivities. The festival has many times been counted among the world's top ten music festivals. In\n[2] Tamworth, New South Wales: popular for birdwatching, Nundle, and Quirindi. Tamworth is best known for hosting the Country Music Festival. The Festival is held over a period of 10 days during January, and is the second biggest country music festival in the world. The festival has many times been counted among the world's top ten music festivals. In 2007, \"\"Forbes\"\" rated it as number 8 of the World's Coolest Music Festivals. It features thousands of Australian and international country music artists performing live shows 24 hours a day. Each year, an estimated 100,000 people pass through Tamworth for the festival, with around 70,000 staying\n[3] Tamworth Country Music Festival: Country Music Association (CCMA), began a talent quest on the Australia Day January Long weekend. The talent quest, now known as the CCMA National Talent Quest, is considered a major influence in what was to become the Festival in January 1973 with the first staging, by local radio station 2TM, of the Australasian Country Music Awards (aka the Golden Guitar Awards for its unique \"\"golden guitar\"\" trophy) as part of its Country Music Capital promotion which had commenced in 1969. The festival expanded to many other activities, with events running back throughout the week before the Awards and National Talent", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 428, "prompt_tokens": 770, "completion_tokens": 92, "retrieval_scores": [0.8914520740509033, 0.8577425479888916, 0.8573850393295288]}, {"t": 3, "action_type": "answer", "query_or_answer": "Tamworth Country Music Festival", "obs_digest": "", "draft": "Tamworth Country Music Festival", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 1.0, "raw_len": 282, "prompt_tokens": 1330, "completion_tokens": 59, "retrieval_scores": []}], "answered_at": 3, "forced_stop": false, "final_answer": "Tamworth Country Music Festival", "final_f1": 1.0, "final_em": 1.0, "steps_used": 3, "total_steps_run": 3, "rollout": 0}
{"task_id": "5abb16415542992ccd8e7f0d", "question": "What was the nationality of Marco Garibaldi's former partner?", "arm": "a3", "mode": "none", "budget_B": 2, "seed": 42, "config_hash": "7e4648315a26", "steps": [{"t": 1, "action_type": "search", "query_or_answer": "Marco Garibaldi former partner", "obs_digest": "[1] Marco Garibaldi: was doing business with Neil when Garibaldi invited Neil to his home. Garibaldi and Presley, from time to time, let Neil stay in the couple's guest quarters when he was \"\"in between wives - and homes\"\". Garibaldi's relationship with Presley ended in 2006. Marco Garibaldi Marco Garibaldi is an American entrepreneur. He is also the former partner of Priscilla Presley and father of Navarone Garibaldi. In 2008, Garibaldi formed a production company under the name of Godfather Entertainment, with its mission being making movies in the $20 million range. The first film to be developed was \"\"The Party\"\", a remake\n[2] Marco Garibaldi: Jesse Mittelstadt. Garibaldi met Presley in 1984 when a mutual friend recommended Garibaldi as a potential screenwriter for a project. That same year, Garibaldi and Presley moved in together and continued to live together in Los Angeles until 2006. The two had a son, Navarone Garibaldi, in 1987. In 1988, Presley stated, \"\"We've both been married before and we both feel that a marriage contract doesn't make it any better or worse. Marriage is somewhat of a business, and as of now our relationship is not a business\"\". Garibaldi was the one who first introduced Vince Neil to Presley. Garibaldi\n[3] Marco Garibaldi: Marco Garibaldi Marco Garibaldi is an American entrepreneur. He is also the former partner of Priscilla Presley and father of Navarone Garibaldi. In 2008, Garibaldi formed a production company under the name of Godfather Entertainment, with its mission being making movies in the $20 million range. The first film to be developed was \"\"The Party\"\", a remake of \"\"The Party\"\" with Peter Sellers. Projects to follow were \"\"Last Chance Motel\"\" and \"\"The Vault\"\". \"\"Last Chance Motel\"\" is a psychological thriller in partnership with Avi Lerner's Nu Image Films, while \"\"The Vault\"\" is a mob movie written by Alex Merkin and", "draft": "EMPTY_DRAFT", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 0.0, "raw_len": 257, "prompt_tokens": 261, "completion_tokens": 59, "retrieval_scores": [0.8420202732086182, 0.8336521983146667, 0.8275097012519836]}, {"t": 2, "action_type": "answer", "query_or_answer": "American", "obs_digest": "", "draft": "American", "draft_f1_vs_gold": 1.0, "raw_len": 345, "prompt_tokens": 819, "completion_tokens": 79, "retrieval_scores": []}], "answered_at": 2, "forced_stop": false, "final_answer": "American", "final_f1": 1.0, "final_em": 1.0, "steps_used": 2, "total_steps_run": 2, "rollout": 0}
